This isn’t easy. Subsequences start with strings of length 0, 1, and the length of S, which may be 2000. Build DP matrices to store the number of distinct subsequences of sub-S’s lengths, and for each length i, compute the distinct subsequences to generate for sub-S of length i. How many comes from? From the distinct subsequences to generate for sub-S of length i-1 (ignore S[i]), and then add in the distinct ones by ignoring S[i]—there are multiple ways to do that. Tail recursion too—find the amount for lengths less than i-1 and build one way to do that exactly now in O(N) loop time, while keeping track of from which state you came from. Modulo 1e9+7 and crazy overflows are my job.
